MIT License

Copyright (c) 2024–2026 TA3HRJ (Erhan)

Three contributions this project is built on.

  TA3PKS (Burak) — the original Rust implementation, and with it the
  extension system the project still runs on: the Extension interface,
  the registry, the extension server, and the own-writer channel that
  lets an extension transmit without having been spoken to first. The
  first logger, fixed-beacon, Twitter and email extensions are that work
  too. The Python port kept the design unchanged, and every extension
  written since — including the AI Gateway — plugs into it.
  https://github.com/ta3pks/aprs-agent

  TA3EKM (Arda Yalın Özkan) — the bidirectional AI Gateway. A station
  that could answer, and not merely report, is what turned this project
  from a one-way logger into a two-way service; it is the hinge the
  architecture turns on, and every extension added afterwards follows
  that pattern.
  https://github.com/ArdaYalinOzkan/aprs-ai-gateway

  TA3HRJ (Erhan) — the original concept, the Python port, and the work
  since: the desktop and web interfaces, station intelligence, the
  silence map and its incident response, RF propagation tracking, and
  the Telegram, WhatsApp, Bluesky and IMAP extensions.
  https://github.com/TA3HRJ/aprs-agent

